  "body": "With side outside (or auto) the entry `ramp`, `helix` and `arc` is ignored for ramp and\r\nhelix. The wall side posts a straight plunge at the lead-in on each level, at the plunge\r\nfeed, and says \"needs bounded air only a bore (Side::Inside) has\". Only the bore side\r\n(`contour_bore.rs`, #1664) ramps.\r\n\r\nThe only way to avoid the plunge today is a workaround: links `level: keep_down`,\r\n`transition: ramp`, `ramp_angle: N`, `approach.ramp_angle: N`, or a Top Z one stepdown\r\nabove the stock.\r\n\r\nNeeded: an outside contour ramps onto its first level and onto each later level. The ramp\r\nruns along the lead-in and the ring. Every point of that path is cut at full depth\r\nafterwards, so the ramp does not need a chord proved over the grown region (which holds\r\nthe part). A helix has no bounded air on the wall side: it stands down to the same\r\nramp, and a note says so once. A tabbed level, or a path too short for the angle, keeps\r\nthe graze and a note names the reason.\r\n\r\nDone means:\r\n- An outside contour with entry ramp and angle 5 posts no feed descent steeper than 5\r\n  degrees, on every level, and no plunge move.\r\n- The default entry (plunge) posts the same moves as before.\r\n\r\nProposed labels (a collaborator sets them): enhancement, source:agent, P6, effort:high, area:2d\r\n",
